  "plan": {
    "data_processing_and_feature_engineering": "Change #1: [Category: Data Augmentation / Feature Engineering] - What: Add a frozen pretrained ResNet18 feature extractor on the leaf images. Load images, resize to 224x224, normalize with ImageNet stats, and extract 512-dim features from the penultimate layer (the average pooling output) using a pretrained model. These features are appended as new columns to the existing tabular feature set. - Why: The current solution completely ignores the provided leaf images, which encode shape, margin, and texture information in raw pixel form. A pretrained CNN can capture high-level visual patterns that complement the handcrafted 64-dim histograms, providing a richer representation and breaking the validation loss plateau. - How: Use timm to load resnet18 (pretrained=True), set to eval mode, and extract features for all train/test images. Concatenate these 512 features with the engineered tabular features before scaling. Ensure split-first: extract features on the full dataset without using labels (unsupervised), then apply StandardScaler fit on training fold only. Preserve the original feature groups for the multi-branch model.",
    "model_design": "Change #2: [Category: Model Architecture] - What: Extend LeafClassificationModel to accept an additional input: the 512-dim image features. Add a dedicated vision encoder branch (a small MLP with LayerNorm, GELU, and dropout) that maps image features to the same hidden_dim (192) as the margin/shape/texture encoders. Incorporate this embedding into the self-attention fusion (i.e., four group embeddings instead of three) and adjust the fusion output and classifier input dimension accordingly (hidden_dim * 4 for concatenation). - Why: The overarching goal is to leverage visual information from the images. A separate vision branch allows the model to learn non-linear combinations of deep features alongside tabular features, while the self-attention fusion learns dynamic weighting across all four modalities. This architecture directly addresses the plateau by providing additional discriminative signal. - How: Modify LeafFeatureEncoder to be reused for vision features. Update SelfAttentionFusion to accept 4 embeddings. In forward(), accept an additional `image_features` argument, encode it, pass to fusion, and concatenate with the max-pooled embeddings and cross-correlation embedding. Keep the classifier width (hidden_dim) and label smoothing (0.1) unchanged. Ensure checkpoint compatibility by initializing fresh weights.",
